From e97517278bf3c0314b84116d9d926faa20dc9b93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:36:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: lossless BF16 TC unembed with fused softcap, opt-in
 FP8 sampled head, batched drawRows

Commit 3 (Lever 3, zero extra VRAM, 100% lossless default):
- Add lossless row-major BF16 Tensor Core unembed kernels (tf_ink2_unembed_tc16 and
  tf_ink2_unembed_tc32, double-buffered cp.async + m16n8k16 MMA) with fused A9(a)
  BF16-round + FP32 softcap epilogue, reading resident row-major m.w.unembed once across
  up to 32 rows (TF_INKLING2_UNEMBED_TC=1 default, 0 reverts to scalar rowdot).
- Add opt-in TF_INKLING2_SAMPLED_FP8_HEAD=1 (default 0) reusing resident m.lazy_head.weight
  (461 MB FP8 qmmf, zero extra VRAM) + fused tf_ink2_round_softcap for fast A/B testing.
- Batch verify taps copies into one tf_ink2_copy_spans launch, batch unmasked greedy top1
  into one launch, and batch unmasked sampled verify rows into one ops.tobf + sliced
  Draws.drawRows (tf_draw_slice_top + tf_draw_rows_finish across 25 vocab slices) using
  post-forward m.s.raw scratch (zero extra VRAM).
